From 5fe3e3f78d983feee9924ee9c758c9778ba1a272 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: W1nkelm4nn <mrmarkap61@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 01:51:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] kk: Support 64-bit atomics on Apple9 GPUs

Metal has 64-bit atomic min and max, unsigned and without returning the
old value, on device memory and on RG32Uint textures read as ulong, from
the Apple9 family on. That is what Unreal Engine 5's Nanite needs for its
visibility buffer, and with it vkd3d-proton can report shader model 6.6
and 64-bit atomics on typed resources.

Expose shaderBufferInt64Atomics and VK_EXT_shader_image_atomic_int64,
with R64_UINT and R64_SINT storage images backed by RG32Uint. Storage
images of RG32 that may be viewed in another format get atomic usage too,
since vkd3d views them as R64 for 64-bit atomics.

Non-returning umin and umax are native. Add, and, or and xor on buffers
are two 32-bit atomics, which leave the right value in memory but may
return a torn old value. The remaining operations, and all others on
images, are reads and writes done one lane of the SIMD group after the
other, so they only race between SIMD groups.

vkd3d-proton's test_shader_sm66_64bit_atomics passes on an M3 (root
descriptors, raw and typed descriptor tables, 96 checks); groupshared
64-bit atomics stay unsupported. In the whole suite, compared with the
build before, only tests that now run instead of being skipped fail
(vkd3d also reports sampler feedback once 64-bit image atomics exist;
three of its tests fail one check each).

Generated-by: LLM
